<KoopsPostLayout
    title="I went too far, so you don’t have to"
    description="A field-note format for the rabbit hole, the hot take, and the extremely specific verdict nobody asked for."
    published="template preview"
    readingTime="6 min side quest"
    heroImage="/images/blog-koops-template-hero.jpg"
    heroAlt="A late-night hobby desk with a translucent controller, cables, magnifying glass, notebook, and blue-orange lighting"
    topics={['deep dives', 'miscellany']}
>
    <p>
        Begin at the exact moment this stopped being a normal interest and became a situation. Be specific. Admit how many tabs were open. The reader is here because you made the questionable decision to keep going.
    </p>

    <h2>Quest log: how we got here</h2>
    <p>
        Set the scene, introduce the thing under investigation, and establish the stakes—even if the stakes are objectively tiny. Especially if the stakes are tiny.
    </p>
    <ol>
        <li>I noticed one suspicious detail.</li>
        <li>I assumed this would take twenty minutes.</li>
        <li>The sun went down.</li>
    </ol>

    <blockquote>
        Current status: technically correct, spiritually somewhere else entirely.
    </blockquote>

    <h2>Inventory check</h2>
    <p>
        Drop the receipts here: comparisons, screenshots, tiny experiments, or the single line of code that caused three hours of emotional damage.
    </p>
    <pre><code>effort += 1;
scope *= 2;
commonSense--;</code></pre>

    <h2>Final boss: the verdict</h2>
    <p>
        Give the opinion cleanly. Say who should care, who can safely ignore all of this, and whether you would willingly enter the rabbit hole again. Bonus points for a rating system that is useful to absolutely nobody else.
    </p>
</KoopsPostLayout>
